// `Task.cancellation_token()` returns the cancellation token of the lexically
// enclosing `task_group` scope, so cooperative code (loops, cancellable runtime
// APIs) can observe structured cancellation. The group owns the cancel
// capability; this only hands out the read-only observation token, and the
// token must not outlive the `task_group` scope it came from.
//
// It must be called inside a `task_group` block. Calling it in an `async fn`
// with no lexical `task_group` is rejected (RS0412): there is no enclosing
// scope token, so the token would silently never cancel. To give a child task
// the group's token, call this in the `task_group` block and pass the token
// into the async function as a `read CancellationToken` parameter.

pub fn Task.cancellation_token() -> fresh CancellationToken
